WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.063 --> 00:00:03.864
It was almost noon on Thursday.

2
00:00:03.865 --> 00:00:10.620
Roscoe rolled a barrel down Main Street.

3
00:00:10.621 --> 00:00:12.715
Cleo shook her head.

4
00:00:12.716 --> 00:00:17.119
She thought the big dog's plan was just plain silly!

5
00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:20.423
"It won't work," Cleo said.

6
00:00:20.424 --> 00:00:23.248
"It will," Roscoe said.

7
00:00:23.249 --> 00:00:25.640
"I once caught a thief this way.

8
00:00:25.641 --> 00:00:28.996
I chased him past some puppies playing marbles.

9
00:00:28.997 --> 00:00:33.226
He slipped on the marbles and fell flat on his back!"

10
00:00:33.227 --> 00:00:36.319
Cleo rolled her eyes.

11
00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:38.895
"You told me that story already.

12
00:00:38.896 --> 00:00:43.119
But this barrel is full of walnuts, not marbles."

13
00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:50.695
Roscoe chuckled. "It is a food fight, isn't it?"

14
00:00:50.696 --> 00:00:54.468
The Tomato Brothers were waiting at the corral.

15
00:00:54.469 --> 00:00:58.113
A pile of vegetables sat between them.

16
00:00:58.114 --> 00:01:02.032
Roscoe rolled the barrel through the gate.

17
00:01:02.033 --> 00:01:04.712
Then he stood it up.

18
00:01:04.713 --> 00:01:07.613
Rocky held a tomato in each hand.

19
00:01:07.614 --> 00:01:09.785
"We didn't think you were coming."

20
00:01:09.786 --> 00:01:12.841
Roscoe glared at the brothers.

21
00:01:12.842 --> 00:01:15.037
"We're here, alright."

22
00:01:15.038 --> 00:01:19.519
Gus tossed a cabbage back and forth in his paws.

23
00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:24.053
"The fight will start on the count of three."

24
00:01:24.054 --> 00:01:28.072
Roscoe began removing the top of the barrel.

25
00:01:28.073 --> 00:01:32.333
Gus counted. "One, two . . ."

26
00:01:32.334 --> 00:01:35.536
Both raccoons threw their vegetables.

27
00:01:35.537 --> 00:01:37.893
Roscoe and Cleo ducked.

28
00:01:37.894 --> 00:01:41.310
"Hey, no fair!" Cleo yelled.

29
00:01:41.311 --> 00:01:43.698
"You didn't say three!"

30
00:01:43.699 --> 00:01:48.048
Tomatoes, cabbages, and other vegetables flew.

31
00:01:48.049 --> 00:01:51.067
Roscoe and Cleo hid behind the barrel.

32
00:01:51.068 --> 00:01:54.233
The sheriff reached up and removed the top.

33
00:01:54.234 --> 00:01:56.315
"Now!" he shouted.

34
00:01:56.316 --> 00:01:59.703
Cleo pushed the barrel over.

35
00:01:59.704 --> 00:02:02.830
Walnuts spilled out and rolled.

36
00:02:02.831 --> 00:02:07.785
Unfortunately they didn't roll anywhere near those two raccoons!

37
00:02:07.786 --> 00:02:11.384
Cleo and Roscoe ran behind a hay bale.

38
00:02:11.385 --> 00:02:17.839
Cleo groaned. "I knew this wouldn't work!"

39
00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:21.541
Gus ran toward them, holding a big pumpkin.

40
00:02:21.542 --> 00:02:25.422
Suddenly his foot slipped on some walnuts.

41
00:02:25.423 --> 00:02:29.825
"Whoa!" Gus dropped the pumpkin on his toes.

42
00:02:29.826 --> 00:02:34.508
"Ouch!" He hopped up and down, holding his foot.

43
00:02:34.509 --> 00:02:38.817
Then he slipped again—and fell. Crunch!

44
00:02:38.818 --> 00:02:41.518
"Help, Rocky!" Gus yelled.

45
00:02:41.519 --> 00:02:44.854
"My head's stuck in this pumpkin!"

46
00:02:44.855 --> 00:02:49.532
Cleo giggled.

47
00:02:49.533 --> 00:02:52.645
Rocky ran over with an armful of tomatoes.

48
00:02:52.646 --> 00:02:58.825
When he saw his brother, he burst into laughter.

49
00:02:58.826 --> 00:03:01.349
"If only Ma could see you now!"

50
00:03:01.350 --> 00:03:06.200
"Quit laughing and help me!" Gus kicked wildly.

51
00:03:06.201 --> 00:03:09.175
His foot hit Rocky, who then fell too.

52
00:03:09.176 --> 00:03:13.819
He landed face first in his tomatoes.

53
00:03:13.820 --> 00:03:16.184
"Hey!" Rocky snapped.

54
00:03:16.185 --> 00:03:19.328
"You kicked me!" He threw a tomato.

55
00:03:19.329 --> 00:03:24.164
It splattered on the pumpkin.

56
00:03:24.165 --> 00:03:32.804
Cleo and Roscoe calmly walked over.

57
00:03:32.805 --> 00:03:36.846
A moment later the raccoons were in handcuffs.

58
00:03:36.847 --> 00:03:42.962
Cleo shook rotten cabbage leaves off her hat. "Yuck!"

59
00:03:42.963 --> 00:03:48.002
Roscoe grinned as he wiped tomato seeds off his vest.

60
00:03:48.003 --> 00:03:56.929
"Sometimes keeping the peace gets a bit messy."

